# Lies you're told (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Lies you're told"). A line ending in ~lie:<key> is a lie the
# player hears (heard_lie:<key>); a line ending in ~truth:<key> is the truth (knows:<key>). Once a
# player has both, the choice with `callout <key>` shows, tagged [Evidence]. Nobody is punished for
# believing a lie: the truth opens a better answer, and that's the payoff.

conv wanderer.scavenger.chemist
for wanderer:scavenger
when !nmem:sold_chemist
topic "Anywhere still worth looking?"
prio world
voice plain

node start
  say "The chemist's in {here}. Back room, top shelf, behind the till. Nobody's touched it. Clean as a whistle, I swear on my boots." ~lie:scav.chemist
  say "A bit of food and it's yours. The knowing, I mean. The shelf's free. Everyone's hungry out here, and I'm everyone."
  > @buy "Here's a tin. Tell me where exactly." -> sold   cost item:food*1   do nset:sold_chemist; later:6h:scav.came_back
  > @hunter "That door was forced. Boot marks." -> caught_out   if bg:hunter,police
  > @catch "Picked clean on Day 3. I asked." -> caught_out   callout scav.chemist
  > @no "No thanks. Not today." -> hub

node sold
  say "Pleasure doing business. The door at the back sticks, so shoulder it. And mind how you go in there. I mean that part."
  > @back1 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

node caught_out
  say "All right, all right. Picked clean, back room and all. But the vet's on the south road still has bandages in the cupboard under the sink. Honest. That one's free, for the cheek."
  do nset:honest
  > @back2 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

conv wanderer.scavenger.came_back
for wanderer:scavenger
when due:scav.came_back & !nmem:honest
once
greet
voice plain

node start
  say? due:scav.came_back :: "You're back. Did you go to the chemist's? Don't tell me. I can see it on you. Still here, though. Still walking. That's the main thing, isn't it."

conv wanderer.doctor.chemist
for wanderer:doctor
when heard_lie:scav.chemist
topic "Is the chemist's in town worth a look?"
prio reaction
once
voice plain

node start
  say "The chemist's? I cleared it myself, on Day 3. Every shelf, every drawer, the back room too. Whoever told you otherwise wanted a tin more than you did." ~truth:scav.chemist
  > @thanks "Good to know. Thank you." -> hub

conv wanderer.doctor.back_room
for wanderer:doctor
when heard_lie:halcyon.back_room
topic "What happens to Halcyon's volunteers?"
prio reaction
once
voice plain

node start
  say "The ones who don't walk out? There's a room at the back of the lab. A chair by every bed and someone with a clipboard in it, all night." ~truth:halcyon.back_room
  say "They're not cruel. They write everything down, every hour, to the end. That's worse, some days."
  > @thanks "Thank you for telling me." -> hub

# A lie the world tests (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Lies you're told"): the town is picked when the topic
# opens (bind), the lie is about that town, and the truth is learned by walking into it while it's
# thick with them (watch). Then the [Evidence] answer shows, the next time the topic opens.
conv wanderer.trader.quiet_town
for wanderer:trader
topic "Which way's quiet today?"
prio flavour
voice plain

bind target = town:thick_within(2500)

node start
  jump !bound -> nowhere
  say "{bind:target}. Quiet as a church. I came through it this morning. Well. Near it. Past it, at a distance, with the wind behind me." ~lie:trader.quiet@target
  do watch:trader.quiet@target:60
  > @thanks "Thanks. I'll go that way." -> hub
  > @catch "{bind:target}? It's thick with them." -> caught   callout trader.quiet@target
  > @no "I'll find my own way." -> hub

node caught
  say "Is it? Must have changed since. Everything does. I sell things, and quiet's a thing people want to buy. Here, have the truth for free: go round it, by the fields."
  > @back1 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

node nowhere
  say "Every way's the same today. Pick one and keep your head down, and don't take any road past a town with its doors hanging open."
  > @back2 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub
